{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791150098,"nonce":"kzmm/+ZUxX+al06sATUW4push/I=","title":"Release archives ship no static runtime, so an installed ash cannot --build","message":"Reported by ashui-8b on v0.1.4: ash-macos-aarch64.tar.gz (and -dev) hold ash,\nlibhl.dylib, libash_std.dylib, simd.hdll and the wasm runtime objects, and\n`ash --build out prog.hl` fails with \"no static runtime found beside \u003cdir\u003e, or\nin the usual library directories\". Reproduced here with the published v0.1.4\ntarball and a one-line program.\n\naot_link::find_runtime(Runtime::Static) looks for libash_std.a (ash_std.lib on\nWindows) beside the executable, ../lib, /usr/local/lib and /usr/lib; it is not\nembedded in the binary (it would double its size). package_release.sh and the\nWindows package step never copied it, so no release has had it: AOT from an\ninstall worked only for programs that load an HDLL (the shared runtime path).","files":null}]}